# Line endings, declared once for every clone — because a machine setting is not a fact about this
# workspace. Git for Windows ships `core.autocrlf=true` in its SYSTEM config, so a clone there
# rewrites every script to CRLF and a shebang line becomes `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r` — which fails
# with "bad interpreter", naming a file that reads as correct. This file overrides that, so the
# answer travels with the repo instead of depending on who cloned it and where.
#
# THE SAME RULE ON EVERY SYSTEM: LF is not "the Linux ending" here, it is the workspace's ending.
# No platform is the default and none is the exception.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Binaries: never touched, never diffed as text. Declared explicitly rather than left to detection,
# because a misdetected .docx is corrupted silently and academy/ holds 89 of them.
*.docx binary
*.pdf  binary
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.pyc  binary
*.tgz  binary
*.gz   binary
*.zip  binary

# Unzipped OOXML payload: the members of a .docx, extracted. `*.docx binary` above covers the
# archive and says nothing about its contents once they are on disk, so these fifteen were being
# treated as text and carried CRLF into the index — the only tracked files in this repo that ever
# did (b20260901). They are rewritten back into a .docx byte for byte, and core/hooks/vendored.txt
# already declares them as not ours to author. Same rule, said to git.
academy/administration/pda/template_extracted/** -text
